{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c48d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":161,"recorded_at":1780531400000317,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-d5ff-7d20-8dcf-e61f4d16058f"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-d5ff-7d20-8dcf-e61f4d16058f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01d-d5ff-7d20-8dcf-e61f4d16058f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(10040 line(s) above)\n10041|### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\n10042|\n10043|A clone is a derivation, never a move or fork alias. It MUST leave source\n10044|bytes, Session Record, provider ID, lease, workspace authority, task-board\n10045|binding, and native identity unchanged. It creates one new direct Session\n10046|Record 2.0.0, target workspace identity, native identity, and epoch-1 lease.\n10047|The target accepts no input until transaction, target Checkpoint, lineage, and\n10048|optional ordinary resume validation succeed.\n10049|\n10050|#### 13.14.1 Capture and canonical contracts\n10051|\n10052|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains its\n10053|schema/version/omission-rule ID, operation ID, source Environment Tuple, and\n10054|sorted unique entries. Each entry has sanitized native\n10055|key, capture class, byte count, blob ID, Blob Descriptor ID, and extensions.\n10056|It contains no credential, runtime, lock, target, AX lease, or fabricated AX\n10057|Session/Provider identity.\n10058|\n10059|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version/ID,\n10060|operation/bundle, source basis, source Environment Tuple, sanitized Native\n10061|Identity, capture-plan digest, Capture Boundary, Raw Object Manifest ID,\n10062|sorted Capture Items, exact excluded classes, core-derived\n10063|<code>raw_complete</code>, creator/time, and extensions. Source basis is\n10064|<code>ax_session</code> with source Session/Record/Checkpoint/Provider Identity\n10065|IDs or <code>external_native</code> with a sanitized source reference.\n10066|\n10067|Each Capture Item has one native key and class\n10068|<code>durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>.\n10069|It is <code>included</code> with descriptor/count and no reason, or\n10070|<code>excluded</code> with null content fields and a stable reason. Credential,\n10071|auth, runtime, and lock classes are excluded. Unknown makes raw completeness\n10072|false and blocks maximal-safe.\n10073|\n10074|Capture Boundary is <code>stable</code> with Stable Snapshot Proof, or\n10075|<code>unstable_archive</code> with generation, pre/post digests,\n10076|<code>source_not_quiescent</code>, explicit acknowledgement, and\n10077|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>. Stable proof records\n10078|<code>closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10079|generation, optional immutable identity, equal pre/post digests, and\n10080|input/foreground/background idle facts. Size equality is never proof. The\n10081|unstable form is core-created only for archive-only output and cannot enter a\n10082|target branch.\n10083|\n10084|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10085|logical Session UUIDv7, source Environment Tuple/native ID, nullable title,\n10086|closed Workspace Binding, 1..1024 Actors, 1..1,000,000 ordered unique Event\n10087|IDs, 1..1024 head IDs, nullable source created/updated times, and extensions.\n10088|Actor contains exactly actor UUIDv7, <code>main|subagent|external</code>,\n10089|nullable parent (null only for main), nullable name/source-native ID/model, and\n10090|extensions.\n10091|\n10092|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10093|logical Session UUIDv7, zero-based contiguous ordinal, 0..64 sorted unique\n10094|causal parents, Actor UUIDv7, nullable turn UUIDv7, kind, nullable source time,\n10095|<code>public|projection|internal|opaque</code> visibility, kind-selected closed\n10096|payload, Source Evidence, and extensions. Source Evidence contains environment\n10097|and native Session IDs, nullable native Event ID/type, sorted unique raw\n10098|blob/manifest byte-range references,\n10099|<code>exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code> capture status, and stable\n10100|reason codes. Synthesized events have no native Event ID and identify the core\n10101|operation.\n10102|\n10103|The exact event kinds are\n10104|<code>session_started|instruction_snapshot|user_message|assistant_message|reasoning_summary|opaque_reasoning|tool_definition_snapshot|tool_call|tool_result|approval_request|approval_response|plan_update|progress|usage|rate_limit|file_change|compaction|turn_started|turn_completed|turn_aborted|subagent_started|subagent_completed|error|migration_checkpoint|session_finished|opaque_event</code>.\n10105|Payloads contain only their registered typed facts. Message-like payloads use\n10106|exactly <code>text|json|image|audio|document|resource_link|redacted|opaque</code>\n10107|content blocks with typed inline content or Blob Descriptor references; inline\n10108|content is at most 64 KiB. Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque\n10109|events. Historical tools\n10110|are inert; incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action.\n10111|Foreign instructions are low-authority history, foreign encrypted/signed\n10112|reasoning is opaque-preserved, and source usage is not target accounting.\n10113|\n10114|The following closed shapes govern this subsection; the preceding prose is a\n10115|summary and does not permit omitted or additional members.\n10116|\n10117|<code>NativeIdentity</code> contains exactly\n10118|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10119|<code>identity_kind:provider_native|official_import|continuation_context</code>,\n10120|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10121|<code>backend_realm_fingerprint:digest|null</code>,\n10122|<code>opaque_identity:string[1..512]|null</code>, and\n10123|<code>extensions</code>. It contains no credential, absolute source path as\n10124|cross-host identity, PID, socket, token, or secret environment value.\n10125|\n10126|<code>WorkspaceBinding</code> contains exactly\n10127|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10128|<code>cwd_relative:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10129|<code>repository_remote_fingerprints:sorted unique digest[0..128]</code>,\n10130|<code>branch:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10131|<code>head_digest:digest|null</code>, <code>index_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10132|<code>working_tree_digest:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10133|The relative cwd is normalized beneath the Workspace Group root; no member\n10134|grants filesystem authority.\n10135|\n10136|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10137|\n10138|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10139|| --- | --- |\n10140|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-raw-object-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10141|| <code>raw_object_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10142|| <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation |\n10143|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact probed <code>EnvironmentTuple</code> |\n10144|| <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Sanitized string[1..512], never an AX Session ID |\n10145|| <code>source_identity_digest</code> | Terminal digest of canonical sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> bytes |\n10146|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Exact core-validated capture-plan digest |\n10147|| <code>entries</code> | <code>RawObjectEntry[0..65536]</code>, sorted unique by native item key |\n10148|| <code>total_bytes</code> | uint53 equal to the sum of entry byte counts |\n10149|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys with no normative reference |\n10150|\n10151|<code>RawObjectEntry</code> contains exactly\n10152|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10153|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|unknown</code>,\n10154|<code>byte_count:uint53</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, and\n10155|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>. The descriptor agrees with blob ID and\n10156|byte count. Credential, machine-auth, runtime-state, transient-lock, and\n10157|excluded candidates are forbidden.\n10158|\n10159|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10160|\n10161|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10162|| --- | --- |\n10163|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-capture-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10164|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10165|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation / logical bundle chain |\n10166|| <code>source_basis</code> | Closed Capture Source Basis below |\n10167|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_identity</code> | Exact tuple / sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> |\n10168|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Terminal digest of the complete canonical capture-plan success body |\n10169|| <code>capture_boundary</code> | Closed Capture Boundary below |\n10170|| <code>source_raw_object_manifest_id</code> | Exact raw manifest containing all and only included objects |\n10171|| <code>items</code> | <code>CaptureItem[0..65536]</code>, sorted bytewise by native item key; one per plan candidate |\n10172|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | Sorted unique capture-class[0..9], exactly the excluded-row classes |\n10173|| <code>raw_complete</code> | Core-derived boolean; true only after complete plan/object reconciliation |\n10174|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> / <code>created_at</code> | UUIDv7 / diagnostic timestamp |\n10175|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10176|\n10177|Capture Source Basis is a closed union. <code>kind=ax_session</code> contains\n10178|exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10179|<code>source_session_record_id:digest</code>,\n10180|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10181|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, and\n10182|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=external_native</code> contains exactly\n10183|<code>kind</code>, <code>external_source_ref:string[1..512]</code>, and\n10184|<code>extensions</code>.\n10185|\n10186|<code>CaptureItem</code> contains exactly\n10187|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10188|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>,\n10189|<code>disposition:included|excluded</code>,\n10190|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest|null</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n10191|<code>exclusion_reason:string[1..128]|null</code>, and\n10192|<code>extensions</code>. Included requires both content members non-null and a\n10193|null reason. Excluded requires null content members and a non-null reason.\n10194|Credential, auth, runtime, and lock classes are always excluded. Unknown makes\n10195|<code>raw_complete=false</code> and blocks <code>maximal_safe</code>.\n10196|\n10197|Capture Boundary is a closed union. <code>kind=stable</code> contains exactly\n10198|<code>kind</code>, <code>proof:StableSnapshotProof</code>, and\n10199|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=unstable_archive</code> contains exactly\n10200|<code>kind</code>, <code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10201|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10202|<code>reason_code=source_not_quiescent</code>,\n10203|<code>operator_explicit=true</code>,\n10204|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10205|Only core may construct the unstable archive form; G2 always rejects it.\n10206|\n10207|<code>StableSnapshotProof</code> contains exactly\n10208|<code>proof_kind:closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10209|<code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10210|<code>snapshot_identity_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10211|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10212|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n10213|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Capture\n10214|digests are equal. Closed-store/provider-quiescence requires all booleans true\n10215|and null snapshot identity; immutable-snapshot/log-prefix requires non-null\n10216|identity. File-size equality is never proof.\n10217|\n10218|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10219|\n10220|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10221|| --- | --- |\n10222|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:canonical-session</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10223|| <code>canonical_session_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10224|| <code>logical_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 stable within bundle lineage |\n10225|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Exact tuple / string[1..512] |\n10226|| <code>title</code> | string[1..4096] or null |\n10227|| <code>workspace</code> | Closed <code>WorkspaceBinding</code> |\n10228|| <code>actors</code> | <code>Actor[1..1024]</code>, unique by actor ID |\n10229|| <code>event_ids</code> | Ordered unique digest[1..1000000] |\n10230|| <code>head_event_ids</code> | Sorted unique digest[1..1024], all in event IDs |\n10231|| <code>created_at</code> / <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp or null |\n10232|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10233|\n10234|<code>Actor</code> contains exactly <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10235|<code>kind:main|subagent|external</code>,\n10236|<code>parent_actor_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>name:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10237|<code>source_native_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10238|<code>model:string[1..512]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Exactly one\n10239|actor is <code>main</code>; only it has null parent.\n10240|\n10241|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n10242|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>event_id</code>,\n10243|<code>logical_session_id</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n10244|<code>parents:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>, <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10245|<code>turn_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>kind</code>,\n10246|<code>timestamp:timestamp|null</code>,\n10247|<code>visibility:public|projection|internal|opaque</code>,\n10248|<code>payload</code>, <code>source_evidence</code>, and\n10249|<code>extensions</code>. Schema/version are exact canonical-event 1.0.0 and\n10250|event ID is the JCS digest with only itself omitted. Ordinals are contiguous\n10251|from zero.\n10252|\n10253|<code>SourceEvidence</code> contains exactly\n10254|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10255|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10256|<code>native_event_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10257|<code>native_type:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10258|<code>raw_refs:sorted unique RawReference[0..65536]</code>,\n10259|<code>capture_status:exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code>,\n10260|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10261|<code>core_operation_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10262|<code>RawReference</code> contains exactly <code>manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10263|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>, and\n10264|<code>length:uint53</code>. Synthesized requires null native Event ID and a\n10265|non-null core operation; all other statuses require null core operation.\n10266|\n10267|#### 13.14.2 Fidelity, projection, and lineage\n10268|\n10269|The dispositions are <code>exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>.\n10270|Every non-exact row names one or more of the closed core reasons\n10271|<code>target_no_equivalent|source_not_persisted|source_truncated|source_corrupt|foreign_encrypted_payload|foreign_signature_unverifiable|target_schema_constraint|target_context_limit|target_size_limit|target_version_gate|official_importer_loss|graph_flattened|unsafe_pending_action|credential_excluded|secret_policy|operator_policy|unsupported_media_type|unknown_native_event|derived_index_rebuilt</code>,\n10272|or a reverse-DNS extension reason that cannot redefine a core code.\n10273|Every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion; every\n10274|raw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition; every canonical\n10275|item to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition. Fidelity Report\n10276|1.0.0 records archive/target scope, profile, tuples, per-item mappings, counts\n10277|by kind/block/bytes/disposition/reason, completeness, semantic continuity,\n10278|native resumability, evidence IDs, and extensions. An aggregate score cannot\n10279|replace item gates.\n10280|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c48f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":162,"recorded_at":1780531400000319,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-d5ff-7d20-8dcf-e61f4d16058f"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-d5ff-7d20-8dcf-e61f4d16058f","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b01d-d5ff-7d20-8dcf-e61f4d16058f"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c491","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":163,"recorded_at":1780531400000321,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01dd1e675b7bedd77f358f2d4c3","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(10040 line(s) above)\n10041|### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\n10042|\n10043|A clone is a derivation, never a move or fork alias. It MUST leave source\n10044|bytes, Session Record, provider ID, lease, workspace authority, task-board\n10045|binding, and native identity unchanged. It creates one new direct Session\n10046|Record 2.0.0, target workspace identity, native identity, and epoch-1 lease.\n10047|The target accepts no input until transaction, target Checkpoint, lineage, and\n10048|optional ordinary resume validation succeed.\n10049|\n10050|#### 13.14.1 Capture and canonical contracts\n10051|\n10052|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains its\n10053|schema/version/omission-rule ID, operation ID, source Environment Tuple, and\n10054|sorted unique entries. Each entry has sanitized native\n10055|key, capture class, byte count, blob ID, Blob Descriptor ID, and extensions.\n10056|It contains no credential, runtime, lock, target, AX lease, or fabricated AX\n10057|Session/Provider identity.\n10058|\n10059|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version/ID,\n10060|operation/bundle, source basis, source Environment Tuple, sanitized Native\n10061|Identity, capture-plan digest, Capture Boundary, Raw Object Manifest ID,\n10062|sorted Capture Items, exact excluded classes, core-derived\n10063|<code>raw_complete</code>, creator/time, and extensions. Source basis is\n10064|<code>ax_session</code> with source Session/Record/Checkpoint/Provider Identity\n10065|IDs or <code>external_native</code> with a sanitized source reference.\n10066|\n10067|Each Capture Item has one native key and class\n10068|<code>durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>.\n10069|It is <code>included</code> with descriptor/count and no reason, or\n10070|<code>excluded</code> with null content fields and a stable reason. Credential,\n10071|auth, runtime, and lock classes are excluded. Unknown makes raw completeness\n10072|false and blocks maximal-safe.\n10073|\n10074|Capture Boundary is <code>stable</code> with Stable Snapshot Proof, or\n10075|<code>unstable_archive</code> with generation, pre/post digests,\n10076|<code>source_not_quiescent</code>, explicit acknowledgement, and\n10077|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>. Stable proof records\n10078|<code>closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10079|generation, optional immutable identity, equal pre/post digests, and\n10080|input/foreground/background idle facts. Size equality is never proof. The\n10081|unstable form is core-created only for archive-only output and cannot enter a\n10082|target branch.\n10083|\n10084|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10085|logical Session UUIDv7, source Environment Tuple/native ID, nullable title,\n10086|closed Workspace Binding, 1..1024 Actors, 1..1,000,000 ordered unique Event\n10087|IDs, 1..1024 head IDs, nullable source created/updated times, and extensions.\n10088|Actor contains exactly actor UUIDv7, <code>main|subagent|external</code>,\n10089|nullable parent (null only for main), nullable name/source-native ID/model, and\n10090|extensions.\n10091|\n10092|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10093|logical Session UUIDv7, zero-based contiguous ordinal, 0..64 sorted unique\n10094|causal parents, Actor UUIDv7, nullable turn UUIDv7, kind, nullable source time,\n10095|<code>public|projection|internal|opaque</code> visibility, kind-selected closed\n10096|payload, Source Evidence, and extensions. Source Evidence contains environment\n10097|and native Session IDs, nullable native Event ID/type, sorted unique raw\n10098|blob/manifest byte-range references,\n10099|<code>exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code> capture status, and stable\n10100|reason codes. Synthesized events have no native Event ID and identify the core\n10101|operation.\n10102|\n10103|The exact event kinds are\n10104|<code>session_started|instruction_snapshot|user_message|assistant_message|reasoning_summary|opaque_reasoning|tool_definition_snapshot|tool_call|tool_result|approval_request|approval_response|plan_update|progress|usage|rate_limit|file_change|compaction|turn_started|turn_completed|turn_aborted|subagent_started|subagent_completed|error|migration_checkpoint|session_finished|opaque_event</code>.\n10105|Payloads contain only their registered typed facts. Message-like payloads use\n10106|exactly <code>text|json|image|audio|document|resource_link|redacted|opaque</code>\n10107|content blocks with typed inline content or Blob Descriptor references; inline\n10108|content is at most 64 KiB. Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque\n10109|events. Historical tools\n10110|are inert; incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action.\n10111|Foreign instructions are low-authority history, foreign encrypted/signed\n10112|reasoning is opaque-preserved, and source usage is not target accounting.\n10113|\n10114|The following closed shapes govern this subsection; the preceding prose is a\n10115|summary and does not permit omitted or additional members.\n10116|\n10117|<code>NativeIdentity</code> contains exactly\n10118|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10119|<code>identity_kind:provider_native|official_import|continuation_context</code>,\n10120|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10121|<code>backend_realm_fingerprint:digest|null</code>,\n10122|<code>opaque_identity:string[1..512]|null</code>, and\n10123|<code>extensions</code>. It contains no credential, absolute source path as\n10124|cross-host identity, PID, socket, token, or secret environment value.\n10125|\n10126|<code>WorkspaceBinding</code> contains exactly\n10127|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10128|<code>cwd_relative:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10129|<code>repository_remote_fingerprints:sorted unique digest[0..128]</code>,\n10130|<code>branch:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10131|<code>head_digest:digest|null</code>, <code>index_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10132|<code>working_tree_digest:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10133|The relative cwd is normalized beneath the Workspace Group root; no member\n10134|grants filesystem authority.\n10135|\n10136|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10137|\n10138|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10139|| --- | --- |\n10140|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-raw-object-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10141|| <code>raw_object_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10142|| <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation |\n10143|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact probed <code>EnvironmentTuple</code> |\n10144|| <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Sanitized string[1..512], never an AX Session ID |\n10145|| <code>source_identity_digest</code> | Terminal digest of canonical sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> bytes |\n10146|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Exact core-validated capture-plan digest |\n10147|| <code>entries</code> | <code>RawObjectEntry[0..65536]</code>, sorted unique by native item key |\n10148|| <code>total_bytes</code> | uint53 equal to the sum of entry byte counts |\n10149|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys with no normative reference |\n10150|\n10151|<code>RawObjectEntry</code> contains exactly\n10152|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10153|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|unknown</code>,\n10154|<code>byte_count:uint53</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, and\n10155|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>. The descriptor agrees with blob ID and\n10156|byte count. Credential, machine-auth, runtime-state, transient-lock, and\n10157|excluded candidates are forbidden.\n10158|\n10159|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10160|\n10161|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10162|| --- | --- |\n10163|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-capture-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10164|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10165|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation / logical bundle chain |\n10166|| <code>source_basis</code> | Closed Capture Source Basis below |\n10167|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_identity</code> | Exact tuple / sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> |\n10168|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Terminal digest of the complete canonical capture-plan success body |\n10169|| <code>capture_boundary</code> | Closed Capture Boundary below |\n10170|| <code>source_raw_object_manifest_id</code> | Exact raw manifest containing all and only included objects |\n10171|| <code>items</code> | <code>CaptureItem[0..65536]</code>, sorted bytewise by native item key; one per plan candidate |\n10172|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | Sorted unique capture-class[0..9], exactly the excluded-row classes |\n10173|| <code>raw_complete</code> | Core-derived boolean; true only after complete plan/object reconciliation |\n10174|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> / <code>created_at</code> | UUIDv7 / diagnostic timestamp |\n10175|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10176|\n10177|Capture Source Basis is a closed union. <code>kind=ax_session</code> contains\n10178|exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10179|<code>source_session_record_id:digest</code>,\n10180|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10181|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, and\n10182|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=external_native</code> contains exactly\n10183|<code>kind</code>, <code>external_source_ref:string[1..512]</code>, and\n10184|<code>extensions</code>.\n10185|\n10186|<code>CaptureItem</code> contains exactly\n10187|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10188|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>,\n10189|<code>disposition:included|excluded</code>,\n10190|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest|null</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n10191|<code>exclusion_reason:string[1..128]|null</code>, and\n10192|<code>extensions</code>. Included requires both content members non-null and a\n10193|null reason. Excluded requires null content members and a non-null reason.\n10194|Credential, auth, runtime, and lock classes are always excluded. Unknown makes\n10195|<code>raw_complete=false</code> and blocks <code>maximal_safe</code>.\n10196|\n10197|Capture Boundary is a closed union. <code>kind=stable</code> contains exactly\n10198|<code>kind</code>, <code>proof:StableSnapshotProof</code>, and\n10199|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=unstable_archive</code> contains exactly\n10200|<code>kind</code>, <code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10201|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10202|<code>reason_code=source_not_quiescent</code>,\n10203|<code>operator_explicit=true</code>,\n10204|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10205|Only core may construct the unstable archive form; G2 always rejects it.\n10206|\n10207|<code>StableSnapshotProof</code> contains exactly\n10208|<code>proof_kind:closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10209|<code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10210|<code>snapshot_identity_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10211|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10212|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n10213|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Capture\n10214|digests are equal. Closed-store/provider-quiescence requires all booleans true\n10215|and null snapshot identity; immutable-snapshot/log-prefix requires non-null\n10216|identity. File-size equality is never proof.\n10217|\n10218|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10219|\n10220|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10221|| --- | --- |\n10222|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:canonical-session</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10223|| <code>canonical_session_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10224|| <code>logical_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 stable within bundle lineage |\n10225|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Exact tuple / string[1..512] |\n10226|| <code>title</code> | string[1..4096] or null |\n10227|| <code>workspace</code> | Closed <code>WorkspaceBinding</code> |\n10228|| <code>actors</code> | <code>Actor[1..1024]</code>, unique by actor ID |\n10229|| <code>event_ids</code> | Ordered unique digest[1..1000000] |\n10230|| <code>head_event_ids</code> | Sorted unique digest[1..1024], all in event IDs |\n10231|| <code>created_at</code> / <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp or null |\n10232|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10233|\n10234|<code>Actor</code> contains exactly <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10235|<code>kind:main|subagent|external</code>,\n10236|<code>parent_actor_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>name:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10237|<code>source_native_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10238|<code>model:string[1..512]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Exactly one\n10239|actor is <code>main</code>; only it has null parent.\n10240|\n10241|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n10242|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>event_id</code>,\n10243|<code>logical_session_id</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n10244|<code>parents:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>, <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10245|<code>turn_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>kind</code>,\n10246|<code>timestamp:timestamp|null</code>,\n10247|<code>visibility:public|projection|internal|opaque</code>,\n10248|<code>payload</code>, <code>source_evidence</code>, and\n10249|<code>extensions</code>. Schema/version are exact canonical-event 1.0.0 and\n10250|event ID is the JCS digest with only itself omitted. Ordinals are contiguous\n10251|from zero.\n10252|\n10253|<code>SourceEvidence</code> contains exactly\n10254|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10255|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10256|<code>native_event_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10257|<code>native_type:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10258|<code>raw_refs:sorted unique RawReference[0..65536]</code>,\n10259|<code>capture_status:exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code>,\n10260|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10261|<code>core_operation_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10262|<code>RawReference</code> contains exactly <code>manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10263|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>, and\n10264|<code>length:uint53</code>. Synthesized requires null native Event ID and a\n10265|non-null core operation; all other statuses require null core operation.\n10266|\n10267|#### 13.14.2 Fidelity, projection, and lineage\n10268|\n10269|The dispositions are <code>exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>.\n10270|Every non-exact row names one or more of the closed core reasons\n10271|<code>target_no_equivalent|source_not_persisted|source_truncated|source_corrupt|foreign_encrypted_payload|foreign_signature_unverifiable|target_schema_constraint|target_context_limit|target_size_limit|target_version_gate|official_importer_loss|graph_flattened|unsafe_pending_action|credential_excluded|secret_policy|operator_policy|unsupported_media_type|unknown_native_event|derived_index_rebuilt</code>,\n10272|or a reverse-DNS extension reason that cannot redefine a core code.\n10273|Every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion; every\n10274|raw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition; every canonical\n10275|item to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition. Fidelity Report\n10276|1.0.0 records archive/target scope, profile, tuples, per-item mappings, counts\n10277|by kind/block/bytes/disposition/reason, completeness, semantic continuity,\n10278|native resumability, evidence IDs, and extensions. An aggregate score cannot\n10279|replace item gates.\n10280|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
