{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":192,"recorded_at":1780531400000379,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-e505-7140-a3c2-922c7f56483d"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-e505-7140-a3c2-922c7f56483d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01d-e505-7140-a3c2-922c7f56483d","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3552 line(s) above)\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3556|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3557|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3558|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3559|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3560|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3561|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3562|\n3563|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3564|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3565|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3566|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3567|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3568|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3569|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3570|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3571|\n3572|The closed operation registry is:\n3573|\n3574|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3575|| --- | --- |\n3576|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3577|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3578|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3579|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3580|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3581|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3582|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3583|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3584|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3585|\n3586|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3587|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3588|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3589|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3590|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3591|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3592|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3593|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3594|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3595|every candidate object.\n3596|\n3597|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3598|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3599|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3600|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3601|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3602|\n3603|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3604|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3605|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3606|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3607|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3608|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3609|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3610|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3611|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3612|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3613|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3614|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3615|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3616|  never paths.\n3617|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3618|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3619|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3620|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3621|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3622|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3623|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3624|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3625|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3626|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3627|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3628|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3629|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3630|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3631|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3632|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3633|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3634|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3635|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3636|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3637|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3638|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3639|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3640|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3641|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3642|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3643|\n3644|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3645|\n3646|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3647|| --- | --- | --- |\n3648|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3649|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3650|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3651|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3652|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3653|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3654|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3655|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3656|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3657|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3658|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3659|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3660|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3661|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3662|\n3663|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3664|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3665|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3666|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3667|and never fallback permission.\n3668|\n3669|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3670|\n3671|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3672|| --- | --- |\n3673|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3674|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3675|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3676|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3677|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3678|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3679|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3680|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3681|\n3682|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3683|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3684|\n3685|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3686|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3687|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3688|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3689|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3690|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3691|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3692|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3693|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3694|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3695|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3696|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3697|never contains executable provenance.\n3698|\n3699|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3700|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3701|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3702|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3703|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3704|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3705|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3706|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3707|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3708|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3709|\n3710|Each capability value contains exactly\n3711|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3712|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3713|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3714|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3715|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3716|\n3717|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3718|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3719|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3720|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3721|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3722|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3723|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3724|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3725|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3726|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3727|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3728|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3729|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3730|\n3731|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3732|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3733|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3734|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3735|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3736|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3737|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3738|write.\n3739|\n3740|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3741|\n3742|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3743|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3744|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3745|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3746|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3747|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3748|\n3749|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3750|\n3751|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3752|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3753|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3754|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3755|\n3756|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3757|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3758|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3759|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3760|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3761|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3762|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3763|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3764|shared.\n3765|\n3766|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3767|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3768|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3769|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3770|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3771|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3772|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3773|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3774|uses an empty body.\n3775|\n3776|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3777|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3778|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3779|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3780|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3781|Error 1.2 has\n3782|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":193,"recorded_at":1780531400000381,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-e505-7140-a3c2-922c7f56483d"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-e505-7140-a3c2-922c7f56483d","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b01d-e505-7140-a3c2-922c7f56483d"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":194,"recorded_at":1780531400000383,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-e53a-7282-b4d9-b9b68eb67c50"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-e53a-7282-b4d9-b9b68eb67c50","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01d-e53a-7282-b4d9-b9b68eb67c50","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(4646 line(s) above)\n4647|### 10.1 Record envelope\n4648|\n4649|Session, event, lease, checkpoint, workspace-group, provider-identity, and\n4650|tombstone objects, plus Tombstone Acknowledgements, are immutable identity-\n4651|addressed objects. “Record” in this storage subsection is generic and does not\n4652|assign the RPC <code>record</code> namespace; Section 11.4 is the sole total\n4653|namespace registry. In addition to their schema-specific fields, each MUST include:\n4654|\n4655|- its canonical digest ID;\n4656|- <code>subject_id</code>, the logical session or workspace scope;\n4657|- <code>created_by_host_id</code>;\n4658|- diagnostic <code>created_at</code>; and\n4659|- optional namespaced <code>extensions</code>.\n4660|\n4661|The storage path MUST be derived from the digest, never from an untrusted\n4662|display name. A digest collision or same-ID/different-bytes observation is an\n4663|integrity emergency: both inputs MUST be quarantined and sync MUST stop for the\n4664|affected peer.\n4665|\n4666|### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs\n4667|\n4668|A blob is an uninterpreted byte sequence identified by SHA-256. Blob metadata\n4669|MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path. Before publishing a record that\n4670|references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest,\n4671|and atomically install it in the object store.\n4672|\n4673|Provider/task-board blobs can contain sensitive project history. Logs and\n4674|metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.\n4675|\n4676|Every transferred blob has a Blob Descriptor with schema\n4677|<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be\n4678|sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly\n4679|<code>size</code> bytes:\n4680|\n4681|The descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4682|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4683|<code>descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>,\n4684|<code>size:uint53</code>, <code>media_type:string[1..255]</code>, and\n4685|<code>chunks:BlobChunk[0..32768]</code>. <code>media_type</code> is a lowercase\n4686|ASCII <code>type/subtype</code> without parameters. BlobChunk is closed and\n4687|contains exactly <code>index:uint32</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>,\n4688|<code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and <code>chunk_id:digest</code>. Indexes\n4689|start at zero and increase by one. An empty blob has size zero and no chunks;\n4690|a non-empty blob has at least one.\n4691|\n4692|~~~json\n4693|{\n4694|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:blob\",\n4695|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4696|  \"descriptor_id\": \"sha256:390c8f21900483a010c1cbc3f9be01afebcf6e4da87263ba09fc5776dd6503ee\",\n4697|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4698|  \"size\": 11,\n4699|  \"media_type\": \"application/octet-stream\",\n4700|  \"chunks\": [\n4701|    {\n4702|      \"index\": 0,\n4703|      \"offset\": 0,\n4704|      \"size\": 11,\n4705|      \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4706|    }\n4707|  ]\n4708|}\n4709|~~~\n4710|\n4711|The descriptor ID is its canonical object digest with\n4712|<code>descriptor_id</code> omitted. The example describes the eleven raw bytes\n4713|<code>ax-example\\n</code>, whose unpadded base64url form is\n4714|<code>YXgtZXhhbXBsZQo</code>; the one last-chunk digest therefore equals the\n4715|whole-blob digest. Empty blobs have an empty chunk array. Protocol 1.0.0 permits\n4716|at most 32,768 chunks in one Blob Descriptor, so one blob is at most 128 GiB.\n4717|A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before\n4718|publishing a partial manifest.\n4719|\n4720|### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor\n4721|\n4722|The transfer unit is a fixed 4 MiB chunk except the last chunk. Chunk schema is\n4723|<code>urn:ax:schema:chunk</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n4724|\n4725|The Transfer Chunk Descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4726|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":195,"recorded_at":1780531400000385,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-e53a-7282-b4d9-b9b68eb67c50"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-e53a-7282-b4d9-b9b68eb67c50","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b01d-e53a-7282-b4d9-b9b68eb67c50"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":196,"recorded_at":1780531400000387,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01ddcc174dc88c7a6d672065c5d","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3552 line(s) above)\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3556|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3557|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3558|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3559|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3560|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3561|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3562|\n3563|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3564|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3565|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3566|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3567|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3568|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3569|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3570|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3571|\n3572|The closed operation registry is:\n3573|\n3574|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3575|| --- | --- |\n3576|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3577|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3578|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3579|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3580|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3581|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3582|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3583|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3584|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3585|\n3586|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3587|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3588|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3589|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3590|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3591|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3592|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3593|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3594|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3595|every candidate object.\n3596|\n3597|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3598|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3599|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3600|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3601|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3602|\n3603|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3604|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3605|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3606|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3607|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3608|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3609|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3610|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3611|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3612|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3613|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3614|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3615|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3616|  never paths.\n3617|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3618|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3619|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3620|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3621|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3622|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3623|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3624|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3625|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3626|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3627|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3628|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3629|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3630|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3631|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3632|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3633|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3634|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3635|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3636|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3637|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3638|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3639|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3640|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3641|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3642|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3643|\n3644|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3645|\n3646|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3647|| --- | --- | --- |\n3648|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3649|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3650|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3651|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3652|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3653|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3654|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3655|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3656|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3657|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3658|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3659|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3660|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3661|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3662|\n3663|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3664|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3665|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3666|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3667|and never fallback permission.\n3668|\n3669|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3670|\n3671|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3672|| --- | --- |\n3673|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3674|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3675|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3676|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3677|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3678|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3679|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3680|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3681|\n3682|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3683|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3684|\n3685|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3686|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3687|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3688|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3689|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3690|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3691|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3692|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3693|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3694|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3695|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3696|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3697|never contains executable provenance.\n3698|\n3699|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3700|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3701|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3702|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3703|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3704|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3705|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3706|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3707|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3708|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3709|\n3710|Each capability value contains exactly\n3711|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3712|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3713|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3714|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3715|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3716|\n3717|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3718|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3719|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3720|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3721|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3722|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3723|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3724|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3725|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3726|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3727|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3728|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3729|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3730|\n3731|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3732|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3733|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3734|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3735|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3736|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3737|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3738|write.\n3739|\n3740|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3741|\n3742|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3743|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3744|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3745|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3746|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3747|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3748|\n3749|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3750|\n3751|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3752|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3753|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3754|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3755|\n3756|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3757|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3758|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3759|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3760|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3761|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3762|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3763|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3764|shared.\n3765|\n3766|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3767|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3768|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3769|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3770|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3771|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3772|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3773|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3774|uses an empty body.\n3775|\n3776|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3777|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3778|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3779|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3780|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3781|Error 1.2 has\n3782|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":197,"recorded_at":1780531400000389,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01de07073519aec8f67cd089c73","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(4646 line(s) above)\n4647|### 10.1 Record envelope\n4648|\n4649|Session, event, lease, checkpoint, workspace-group, provider-identity, and\n4650|tombstone objects, plus Tombstone Acknowledgements, are immutable identity-\n4651|addressed objects. “Record” in this storage subsection is generic and does not\n4652|assign the RPC <code>record</code> namespace; Section 11.4 is the sole total\n4653|namespace registry. In addition to their schema-specific fields, each MUST include:\n4654|\n4655|- its canonical digest ID;\n4656|- <code>subject_id</code>, the logical session or workspace scope;\n4657|- <code>created_by_host_id</code>;\n4658|- diagnostic <code>created_at</code>; and\n4659|- optional namespaced <code>extensions</code>.\n4660|\n4661|The storage path MUST be derived from the digest, never from an untrusted\n4662|display name. A digest collision or same-ID/different-bytes observation is an\n4663|integrity emergency: both inputs MUST be quarantined and sync MUST stop for the\n4664|affected peer.\n4665|\n4666|### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs\n4667|\n4668|A blob is an uninterpreted byte sequence identified by SHA-256. Blob metadata\n4669|MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path. Before publishing a record that\n4670|references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest,\n4671|and atomically install it in the object store.\n4672|\n4673|Provider/task-board blobs can contain sensitive project history. Logs and\n4674|metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.\n4675|\n4676|Every transferred blob has a Blob Descriptor with schema\n4677|<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be\n4678|sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly\n4679|<code>size</code> bytes:\n4680|\n4681|The descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4682|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4683|<code>descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>,\n4684|<code>size:uint53</code>, <code>media_type:string[1..255]</code>, and\n4685|<code>chunks:BlobChunk[0..32768]</code>. <code>media_type</code> is a lowercase\n4686|ASCII <code>type/subtype</code> without parameters. BlobChunk is closed and\n4687|contains exactly <code>index:uint32</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>,\n4688|<code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and <code>chunk_id:digest</code>. Indexes\n4689|start at zero and increase by one. An empty blob has size zero and no chunks;\n4690|a non-empty blob has at least one.\n4691|\n4692|~~~json\n4693|{\n4694|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:blob\",\n4695|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4696|  \"descriptor_id\": \"sha256:390c8f21900483a010c1cbc3f9be01afebcf6e4da87263ba09fc5776dd6503ee\",\n4697|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4698|  \"size\": 11,\n4699|  \"media_type\": \"application/octet-stream\",\n4700|  \"chunks\": [\n4701|    {\n4702|      \"index\": 0,\n4703|      \"offset\": 0,\n4704|      \"size\": 11,\n4705|      \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4706|    }\n4707|  ]\n4708|}\n4709|~~~\n4710|\n4711|The descriptor ID is its canonical object digest with\n4712|<code>descriptor_id</code> omitted. The example describes the eleven raw bytes\n4713|<code>ax-example\\n</code>, whose unpadded base64url form is\n4714|<code>YXgtZXhhbXBsZQo</code>; the one last-chunk digest therefore equals the\n4715|whole-blob digest. Empty blobs have an empty chunk array. Protocol 1.0.0 permits\n4716|at most 32,768 chunks in one Blob Descriptor, so one blob is at most 128 GiB.\n4717|A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before\n4718|publishing a partial manifest.\n4719|\n4720|### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor\n4721|\n4722|The transfer unit is a fixed 4 MiB chunk except the last chunk. Chunk schema is\n4723|<code>urn:ax:schema:chunk</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n4724|\n4725|The Transfer Chunk Descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4726|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
