{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c581","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":283,"recorded_at":1780531400000561,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-27e0-7cc0-896d-a90c97e9f1f5"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-27e0-7cc0-896d-a90c97e9f1f5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01e-27e0-7cc0-896d-a90c97e9f1f5","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-8-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"exclusion-handoff\\\\|MatchExcludedFromReplication\\\\|ExcludedConfigDirName\\\" /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/ 2>&1 | head -n 30\\necho \\\"===BOARDRES===\\\"\\ntask-board resource list --help 2>&1 | head -n 20; task-board q --help 2>&1 | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Find exclusion handoff content\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev4.md:7:F3 (P2, rows 15 and 21): native Windows DACL read/install code exists, so the owner-SID-only criticism is closed, but only a pure evaluator plus cross-build/vet exist. Add real native Windows test code (build-tagged) for owner-only acceptance, other-principal refusal and reparse handling driven through the production custody entry points; where no Windows runtime is available, count row 15 as implementation present, runtime evidence unverified — never as a pass. Classify the actual config-backup contents and the custody contract that applies to them instead of claiming profile ACL inheritance proves custody. For row 21, MatchExcludedFromReplication and ExcludedConfigDirName still have only test callers: persist a precise handoff naming each downstream owning task (replication, snapshot, clone, Session Directory, diagnostics), the API each must call and the test obligation each carries, attach it as a task-scoped outcome, add the corresponding board notes on the named owners only through task-board, and count row 21 honestly as not consumer-driven. Do not implement unrelated RPC transport or consumer surfaces that belong to other leaves.\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md:1:Independently review Change Request revision 5 of TASK-260909-2ez769 (task_delta on managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903, candidate tree a823eb20be497c3fa0510e7da4d3506ddb284431, published by RUN-260916-c0f186). This is the rework after the CR4 changes-requested verdict (TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev4.md, evidence zip rev4); read that verdict, the CR4 logbook, the producer outcome TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev5.md with TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev5.tar.gz and TASK-260909-2ez769_exclusion-handoff.md, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. Superseded reviewer briefs (reviewer, reviewer-current-base, reviewer-after-rev3, reviewer-after-rev3-current) are historical; this brief governs.\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev4.md:84:- `MatchExcludedFromReplication` and `ExcludedConfigDirName` still have only\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev4.md:125:|21|Secret exclusion across consumers|MatchExcludedFromReplication/ExcludedConfigDirName / helper tests only|Not consumer-driven; precise ownership handoff incomplete|\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rework.md:18:5. P2 exclusion \\\\u2014 `ExcludedFromReplication` gains pending-commit.json; new `MatchExcludedFromReplication` (staging prefixes, fail-closed escapes) and `ExcludedConfigDirName`; tests walk the whole custody layout (every file excluded), pin published backup names, and keep explicit enrollment export exchangeable. No in-repo replication/snapshot/export-of-state production surface exists (sessadapter/localstore/dirnode verified not to touch host-channel): HANDOFF to future export surfaces \\\\u2014 every replication, snapshot, clone, Session Directory or diagnostic-bundle writer MUST consult `MatchExcludedFromReplication`/`ExcludedConfigDirName` and drop matches, with a negative test per surface that fails when a custody path is admitted. Mutation claim corrected: config kills are 4 semantic narrowing + 1 label-precision (plant text marked LABEL-PRECISION in-table).\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rework.md:44:| 21 | Secret exclusion across export surfaces | hosttrust MatchExcludedFromReplication/ExcludedConfigDirName / walk + name + matcher tests | enforced at custody surface; downstream surfaces get explicit handoff above |\\n===BOARDRES===\\nManage attached resources such as screenshots, docs, logs, and other files.\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board resource add\\\" to create a new attached resource, \\\"task-board\\nresource adopt\\\" to register an orphaned local payload, \\\"task-board resource\\nupdate\\\" to replace an existing one, \\\"task-board resource delete\\\" to remove it,\\nand \\\"task-board resource get\\\" to materialize a resource back to the local\\nfilesystem for inspection.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board resource [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  add         Attach a new file resource to an element\\n  adopt       Register an existing unreferenced local resource payload\\n  delete      Delete a resource from an element (requires --confirm)\\n  get         Download a resource to the local filesystem\\n  update      Replace an existing file resource on an element\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for resource\\nExecute queries against the board using a compact DSL.\\n\\nOperations:\\n  get(ID)              Get a single element by ID\\n  activity(ID, ...)    Read bounded, cursor-paginated element activity\\n  list(filters...)     List elements with filters\\n  count(filters...)    Count elements matching filters\\n  summary()            Board overview (counts + active/blocked)\\n  plan(scope?)         Execution phases; scope=[ID,ID,...] plans the union of subtrees\\n  agents(stale=N?)     Agent dashboard\\n  models(agent?)       Available models for spawn\\n  project_config()     Full active project board runtime config (always local)\\n  project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER?)\\n                       Narrow effective child-spawn policy for one target\\n  provider_limits()    Machine-scoped provider rate-limit state (always local)\\n  provider_limits(identity=KEY|all_identities=true)\\n                       Report one indexed provider identity, or every one\\n  whoami()             Current remote URL and active user (always local)\\n  schema()             Introspect the full operations/fields/presets contract,\\n                       including the statement grammar (arguments, quoting,\\n                       projection, batching) under \\\"grammar\\\"\\n  schema(operation=NAME|mutation=NAME)\\n                       Return only one typed operation or mutation signature\\n                       plus a one-line \\\"syntax\\\" statement of the grammar\\n\\nField projection:\\n  { id status assignee }     Select specific fields\\n  { overview }               Use a base preset (minimal, default, overview, full, progress, planning)\\n  { observability-task }     Use project observability presets (project, epic, story, task)\\n  (omitted)                  Defaults to { id name status }\\n\\nBatching:\\n  Separate multiple queries with semicolons; results preserve source order\\n\\nSpawn policy projection:\\n  Full project_config reports the effective spawn-policy-v2/v3 contract,\\n  authority, normalized provider and role-effective policy, and exact config\\n  provenance. V2 additionally reports its frozen compatibility snapshot and a\\n  copy-ready v3 migration object; this is read-only evidence and never edits\\n  task-board.config.json. Spawn-preflight returns only the selected role policy\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7134,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1784,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
