{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":700,"recorded_at":1780531400001395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01f-598b-7101-81c3-a8591cfdfafb"},"task_id":"01a0b01f-598b-7101-81c3-a8591cfdfafb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01f-598b-7101-81c3-a8591cfdfafb","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-20-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rln \\\"narrowing\\\\|mutant\\\" internal/ --include=\\\"*.go\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" --include=\\\"*.sh\\\" | head -n 20\\necho \\\"===LOGBOOK-HEAD===\\\"; head -n 60 LOGBOOK.md\\necho \\\"===README-STRUCT===\\\"; grep -n \\\"^#\\\\|^##\\\" README.md | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"Find mutant harness pattern and docs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"internal/hosttrust/hold.go\\ninternal/hosttrust/mutations.py\\ninternal/hosttrust/hold_test.go\\ninternal/hosttrust/custody.go\\ninternal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py\\ninternal/resumesmoke/mutant_test.go\\ninternal/cataloggen/generate_test.go\\ninternal/config/extension_canonical_byte_bound_test.go\\ninternal/config/legacy_revalidate_test.go\\ninternal/config/extension_key_admission_test.go\\ninternal/config/hold_test.go\\ninternal/config/endpoint_admission_test.go\\ninternal/config/mutations_v4.py\\ninternal/config/terminal_registry_wiring_test.go\\ninternal/config/loader_home_test.go\\ninternal/config/writepath_census_test.go\\ninternal/config/ssh_admission_test.go\\ninternal/peeridentity/mutations.py\\ninternal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\\ninternal/matjournal/TRACEABILITY.md\\n===LOGBOOK-HEAD===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n  zero duplicate authorized owners) over `sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`,\\n  `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`\\n  (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, v0.6.0). Final leaf of\\n  STORY-260830-1oqfec; carries the story-close traceability,\\n  README, and registry re-pin items.\\n- DEFECT (RED-first): `resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease\\n  against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's\\n  divergent-history evidence — even its presence — depended on union\\n  order (witness: `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain reports the loss in\\n  one arrival order and drops it in the other). FIX: two-pass\\n  resolution — select the greatest tuple first, then report every\\n  entry below it in ascending tuple order naming the final winner,\\n  with the off-chain flag recomputed from the final winner. All\\n  landed union assertions were order-free, so only the refusal-census\\n  line pins moved (sessstate.go:924/927 to :929/:932).\\n- GENERATORS: closed small alphabet, hand-written (no new dependency):\\n  exhaustive multisets of size 0..3 with all permutations and all\\n  ordered 2-partitions over three chain shapes, all `Compare`\\n  pairs/triples against an independent builtin-operator oracle, all\\n  reason sequences of length 0..2, the full presenter/observation/\\n  operation gate table, plus seeded-random union multisets (seed\\n  260830) and reason sequences (seed 260831) with recorded counts.\\n- MUTANTS (`internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py`): 8\\n  narrowing plants (inverted tie-break, first-arrival evidence\\n  target, dropped same-/lower-epoch losers, clock-consulting\\n  creation and expiry, admitted same-epoch loser, admitted remote\\n  holder), each KILLED by its named property; applied harmless\\n  control SURVIVED; not-applied and compile-failure controls\\n  classified separately. The expiry plant is invisible to the landed\\n  suite (all-2026 fixtures) and only the translation property kills\\n  it, which proves the property adds falsification power.\\n- BOUNDS: grant age relative to the refresh policy stays authoritative\\n  by design (only absolute clock position is non-authoritative);\\n  malformed-union refusal evidence names the first malformed entry in\\n  arrival order (order-independence covers well-formed inputs);\\n  no `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is claimed.\\n- TRACEABILITY: three new acceptance cases\\n  (`lease-ownership-union/store/gate-properties`) bound to `Reduce`,\\n  `WinningLease`, and `Authorize`, attached to the discharged 5.3#6,\\n===README-STRUCT===\\n1:# Agent Session Manager (`ax`)\\n6:## Project Status\\n23:## Bootstrap\\n53:## Implementation Plan\\n77:## Normative Source Pin\\n99:## Pinned Specification Document\\n140:## Common Wire Scalar Types\\n196:# exits non-zero: 0/31, 0/3, 0/5, 1/3 and 0/25 normative clauses discharged\\n199:## Configuration Loading and Versioned Schemas\\n393:## Host Trust Store and Configuration 4.0.0\\n447:## Provider Plugin Discovery and Trust\\n491:## Provider Plugin JSONL Protocol\\n586:## Safe Process and Filesystem Primitives\\n685:## Security Conformance Test Instrument\\n775:## Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\\n834:## Canonical JSON and Immutable Object Identities\\n1493:## Safe Local Layout, Immutable Blob Sink, and SQLite Projection\\n1687:## Session Repository and Append-Only Event Chain\\n1814:## Session State Reducer\\n1927:## Execution profiles: derivation, set-profile, and provider mapping\\n2027:## Native-resume smoke: provider checks and tuple refusals\\n2084:## Provider and pane fencing gates\\n2139:## Ownership reducer properties\\n2201:## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\\n2341:## Workspace Checkpoint Records\\n2361:## Materialization Journal and Recovery\\n2386:## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n2416:## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\\n2550:## CLI Result Envelopes, Rendering Boundaries, and Exit Status\\n2644:### Which refusal wins when two apply\\n2677:### What a machine client is allowed to depend on\\n2910:### Refusal guard inventory\\n3000:## Generated Contract Catalogs\\n3044:## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\n3080:### Declared coverage and what the gate can decide\\n3147:### Measured coverage of this repository\\n3317:## Managed Skills\\n3360:## Tools and Outputs\\n3389:## Contribution Baseline\\n3400:## Configured Host and Peer Identity\\n3442:## SSH stdio transport\\n3489:## Mesh RPC envelopes and Host Channel\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8851,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2213,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
