etadata; missing lock; lock release != adopted via a temp root with a v0.5.0 lock copied under the adopted name; stale generated output under -adopted -check), a narrowing mutant per refusal and per the byte-identity claim with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), and a conformance row map to the task AC. Managed Story worktree contract: the worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/STORY-260917-158jyi/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260917-158jyi forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260917-3lt2xv and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). This is the Story's only leaf, so the CR is story_final. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff (your candidate's command 21 and trunk's explicit command 21 must BOTH be green on your tree — construction will run trunk's); hand off no later than 1.5 hours in. Attach TASK-260917-3lt2xv_results.md, TASK-260917-3lt2xv_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260917-3lt2xv --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.\\nTASK-260830-24z2b3_producer.md\\nOwn TASK-260830-24z2b3 (implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types), first leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q (canonical-session-capture-and-evidence, EPIC M4; siblings 2g5be6 and 32ypr2 follow). Implement, as production co