rrectly refuses the stale lock. Fix the contract at the source, not with a workaround: (1) declare the adopted release once in internal/catalog (for example `const Adopted Release = ReleaseV060` next to Current(), with Current() defined through it so the two cannot diverge; add a test pinning Current().Release == Adopted); (2) add an `-adopted` mode to internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen that derives `-metadata internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `-contracts internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` from catalog.Adopted relative to a `-root` (default \\\".\\\" — the validation suite runs from the repository root), refuses `-adopted` combined with explicit -metadata/-contracts, refuses a missing metadata or lock file with distinct messages naming the derived path, refuses a lock whose source release differs from the adopted release before generation, and otherwise behaves byte-identically to the explicit invocation (same Generate call, same -check/-output semantics); (3) switch validation command 21 in task-board.config.json to `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (edit exactly that string in the candidate; never edit the control root; every other command unchanged) and prove it green on the candidate; (4) README tool row for cataloggen documents the -adopted form and the explicit form; LOGBOOK entry. No catalog content, metadata, lock or generated-output change: `git diff --exit-code internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json internal/specpin/` must be empty. Tests drive the production entry (the cataloggen run function / main through os/exec) with positives (-adopted -check green; -adopted generation byte-identical to explicit generation into a temp output; explicit flags still work) and refusals (mixed flags; missing metadata; missing lock; lock release != adopted via a temp root with a v0.5.0 lock copied under the adopted name; stale generated output under -adopted -check), a