nts killed (named), 1 label-precision kill, 2 neutral controls; `go test ./...` all ok; config refusal-inventory + secprim census green.\\nLOGBOOK.md:812:- EVIDENCE: all 26 configured local gates passed; later focused config rework passed and the final handoff reruns the same gates on its captured candidate. Eleven narrowing mutants each produced semantic assertion failures with 11 passing instrumentation controls; token-preserving stale generator directive still passes the static token check and fails the behavioral CLI suite. Mutations ran in a task-scoped copy and were restored byte-exact. One initial M4 applicator failed because instrumentation split its exact needle; that attempt is recorded as setup failure, not a kill, and the corrected battery re-proved all rows. Archived per-command exits supersede the prior unarchived battery claims.\\nLOGBOOK.md:909:- F2 (duplicate class measured at one key): narrowing `duplicate && key != K` survived 6/8 response keys and 7/10 owner keys. Fix: derivation-backed sweepers (member sets derived from tuple/observation/response/scan-request production; new members auto-swept) through `DecodeTuple`/`CheckScanRequest`/`DecodeManifest`/`DecodeResponse`/`DecodeStrictObject`. Battery adds 8 owner + 6 retained narrowing mutants, one per survived key. Survivor honest-report: first `P_dupnarrow_provider_id` run SURVIVED and exposed a real test gap (foreign `provider_id` missing from the envelope sweeper); key added, mutant re-run KILLED.\\nLOGBOOK.md:1202:- EVIDENCE: 26 narrowing mutants (order-skip-first, bound+1, grammar weakening, gate `&&`→`||`, disjunct drops, key widening, registry deletion), each presence-asserted, full-package run, cp-aside restore byte-verified, tree hash equal before/after: 24 killed on first run, 2 survived (order checks skipping index 0 — no fixture distinguished the first element), both killed after adding first-element-substitution fixtures. Final: 26/26, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0, `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases — no ownership bindings added or claimed). provhost cover 86.4% (was 88.1%: the new decoders add the same constructor-error propagation branches the audit already records as the uncovered remainder).\\nLOGBOOK.md:1216:- FIX (F28/F29): orphaned discovery paragraph moved back above the JSONL section; the \\\"proven by narrowing mutants\\\" sentence restated to what the tests pin (arm identities, 31/32 token bytes, both exact frame bounds).\\nLOGBOOK.md:1232:- EVIDENCE: 25 narrowing mutants, each verified present, compiling, and restored — 25 killed, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` exit 0 in batches over all 15, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `gofmt` clean, `tracecheck` exit 0, catalog generate current.\\nLOGBOOK.md:1917:- STATUS: BUG-260902-2faftr, on `task-board/story/STORY-260902-2oiugz` (forked from trunk `67aed0b`, zero commits behind `main` at measurement time); `internal/config` coverage 94.4%, against a 93.9% pre-change measurement taken from a `git archive HEAD` copy (the preservation tests raise it; no statement lost coverage); `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l ./internal`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `go test ./... -cover -count=1`, full and assigned-scope `tracecheck`, and `cataloggen -check` all exit 0; the seven single-clause mutants were re-run on this tree and each exited 1, counting `--- FAIL` subtest lines only (re-added key blacklist reddens 17 of the 20 admission subtests, reproducing the accepted review's measurement exactly; re-added nested-key blacklist 10; dropped grammar gate 11; widened 253-byte key bound 2; widened depth bound 2; dropped registered backend-settings schema call 2; dropped `DisallowUnknownFields` 5), with the tree restored green after each. An eighth mutant closes the review's non-blocking finding: deleting every blacklisted-label nested key from the loaded map passes the whole suite on the previous revision (exit 0) and reddens all 11 preservation subtests here (exit 1). With the preservation tests present the two required narrowing mutants redden more, not less: re-added key blacklist 18, re-added nested-key blacklist 21. Handed off to review. No commit hash is named here: this entry ships in the commit it would describe, so the hash cannot be known when it is written.\\nLOGBOOK.md:2039:- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5497,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1375,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
