{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e157","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7212-75f1-8296-534762977aff"},"sequence":3846,"recorded_at":1780531400007687,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"663d949a-c622-460a-8733-e5cc483c026f"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Handed off to review: `TASK-260830-24z2b3` is `to-review`, checklist 14/14, with `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`, `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`, and `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` attached. Candidate left uncommitted in the Story worktree.\n\nWhat shipped: new `internal/clonebundle` package implementing the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts (Raw Object Manifest, Capture Manifest with items/basis/boundary, Canonical Session/Event, identities, generations), Section 10.2 descriptor agreement plus no-replace install via `localstore`, and the row-21 hosttrust exclusion allowlist at construction. AC coverage 18 of 18 rows driven through named production entries; 17 narrowing mutants killed plus a survived harmless control; package coverage 82.2%.\n\nTwo findings, both in the results evidence: (1) the first full run reddened the provhost no-attestation census — fixed at root cause by using `CalculateObjectIdentity` with a local claim comparison instead of the attesting entry, following the landed sessprofile precedent; (2) `go test -race ./...` at the default 10m timeout leaves untouched `internal/sessquery` red on this host (600s timeout, no data race, no failing assertion) — it passes in 630s with `-timeout 25m`; reported as a finding, with the default-timeout gate honestly red on that package.","reason":null}}
